                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e4f77d37-797c-3b45-b921-9aa58718f998",
                        "entry_id": "f1f276a7-23db-3392-9c3b-86e1fc8196c1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "ж.-д. железнодорожный рабочий, управляющий семафором"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "eee62b71-afc1-3e8e-a209-a7f2acfb907d",
                        "entry_id": "f1f276a7-23db-3392-9c3b-86e1fc8196c1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "морск. тот, кто передаёт и принимает сигналы по семафору"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e72be309-2ad6-434d-a9e9-6747515fcbf1",
                        "source_entry_id": "f1f276a7-23db-3392-9c3b-86e1fc8196c1",
                        "target_lang_word": "semaphore",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "semaphore",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c6239642-caee-3fb3-8760-2c61621d6cd6",
                                        "entry_id": "239c840a-01a9-31e4-8d93-f73af7f7e715",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any equipment used for visual signalling by means of flags, lights, or mechanically moving arms, which are used to represent letters of the alphabet, or words."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e21102a-2040-4456-929d-a0c6ffedf4b3",
                                                "sense_id": "c6239642-caee-3fb3-8760-2c61621d6cd6",
                                                "text": "We must here take the liberty of expostulating with Sir Home [Riggs] Popham and the first Lord of the Admiralty, for having given to the telegraphic machine, invented by that gallant officer, the barbarous name of Semaphore, instead of Sematophore or Semophore—either of them ugly enough."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ce90a786-b6fa-4171-b8b0-80fa3b760d0b",
                                                "sense_id": "c6239642-caee-3fb3-8760-2c61621d6cd6",
                                                "text": "The large Silver Medal of the Society was this Session voted to Nic[h]olas Harris Nicolas, Esq. of the Inner Temple, for an Improvement on the Vertical Semaphore, and for his method of adapting a shifting Key to Telegraphic Communications, for the purpose of insuring their Secrecy. A Model of Mr. N's Semaphore has been placed in the Repository of the Society."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e4f81a32-a8b4-448b-80f3-cb9ada95cfe9",
                                                "sense_id": "c6239642-caee-3fb3-8760-2c61621d6cd6",
                                                "text": "That the systems of telegraph and semaphore now in use are in a great measure use-less by night, and totally so in a fog, cannot be doubted; and that a mode, both rapid and secret, would could be put into practice at small expense, in fact little more than the first cost, would be of essential utility to the Government of the country adopting it, is equally true."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "095a929b-cff2-428a-bcbf-d0ac5af0c50f",
                                                "sense_id": "c6239642-caee-3fb3-8760-2c61621d6cd6",
                                                "text": "The arms of the semaphore at the settlement were, in fact, gesticulating with comical vehemence.",
                                                "translation": "For the Term of His Natural Life",
                                                "english": "For the Term of His Natural Life"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a0cd7597-6270-412e-9ca4-61fb0bbe53f2",
                                                "sense_id": "c6239642-caee-3fb3-8760-2c61621d6cd6",
                                                "text": "When, on long lines of stations, towers or other structures are used, it may be necessary, for greater speed, to sometimes employ semaphores for aerial telegraphy. [...] Semaphores consist of a post with arms. The arms starting with about three feet in length, to be increased one foot for every mile. These arms are made movable by ropes passing over wheels or pulleys, and moved by a crank below."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a544935e-5af0-4e4f-92ed-dee2822c18f6",
                                                "sense_id": "c6239642-caee-3fb3-8760-2c61621d6cd6",
                                                "text": "And so they went down, Jim steering by his father, turn for turn, over the Mayapur Bar, with the semaphores on each bank duly signalling the depth of water, [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8905e468-c423-4e85-a3db-c505282fb67d",
                                                "sense_id": "c6239642-caee-3fb3-8760-2c61621d6cd6",
                                                "text": "It is essentially an emergency device, primarily for use on single track railroads, and is intended to place the control of semaphores at the several stations under the control of the dispatcher. By means of this signal the dispatcher may throw a semaphore to \"stop position\" at any desired point, regardless of the condition of the operator's instrument at that station, that is whether or not the key of his instrument on the dispatcher's wire is open."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ab71a7e-67d4-4bc0-ab34-8425135667cd",
                                                "sense_id": "c6239642-caee-3fb3-8760-2c61621d6cd6",
                                                "text": "Now, a century later, semaphores and discs are giving place to colour and position lights. What will be the fashion in 2041? Universal continuous cab signalling?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0fcd9f22-8a4d-4cc9-a83e-1a878080427a",
                                                "sense_id": "c6239642-caee-3fb3-8760-2c61621d6cd6",
                                                "text": "Travelling by the rural tramway was quite an experience; the small car would bounce about on the bad track like a ship in a rough sea; at some places, there would even be genuine railway semaphore signals controlling the trams."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1db35b6f-4582-4632-b1a5-8b82a1c0dd1e",
                                                "sense_id": "c6239642-caee-3fb3-8760-2c61621d6cd6",
                                                "text": "Innovations in the communications industry often means that existing media become obsolete. There are no semaphores any longer. (Semaphores were used by the French revolutionary armies in the late 1790's to relay information to Paris about their victories in the Savoy.)"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d61c902c-22d6-4208-a81b-7b7acaf44cb1",
                                                "sense_id": "c6239642-caee-3fb3-8760-2c61621d6cd6",
                                                "text": "He had got used to the clacks towers now. Sometimes it seemed as though every roof sprouted one. Most were the new shutter boxes installed by the Grand Trunk Company, but old-fashioned arm semaphores and even signal flags were still well in evidence."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6021f36-b599-4af8-a832-9ecff59cad15",
                                                "sense_id": "c6239642-caee-3fb3-8760-2c61621d6cd6",
                                                "text": "Even so, there are only four others in my car after leaving the pretty station at Abergavenny, a haven of old GWR semaphores."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d58b7504-1253-3337-851b-5427ed53bb65",
                                        "entry_id": "239c840a-01a9-31e4-8d93-f73af7f7e715",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A visual system for transmitting information using the above equipment; especially, by means of two flags held one in each hand, using an alphabetic and numeric code based on the position of the signaller's arms; flag semaphore."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "204aa311-bcf5-4e4f-b7c8-88cfceb6183a",
                                                "sense_id": "d58b7504-1253-3337-851b-5427ed53bb65",
                                                "text": "Its [the article's] object is to furnish a rule for determining the number of distinct signals which can be made by any semaphore, whatever be the number of arms or indicators, of whatever be the number of positions of each arm. In the Cyclopædia of Rees, the number of signals which the semaphores of the line of communication between Paris and Landau were capable of making, is stated to be 823,543, which is no less than 1,274,608 fewer than the real number, an error not arising from the press, but from the principle of computation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5f03f4a6-f464-490b-97dc-d29fd6f63004",
                                                "sense_id": "d58b7504-1253-3337-851b-5427ed53bb65",
                                                "text": "Buried treasures are naturally among the problems which have come to Mr. [Sherlock] Holmes. One genuine case was accompanied by a diagram here reproduced. [...] Each Indiaman in those days had its own semaphore code, and it is conjectured that the three marks upon the left are signals from a three-armed semaphore."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "13192b11-1c6d-4d49-9fd5-0bf38dc5bab0",
                                                "sense_id": "d58b7504-1253-3337-851b-5427ed53bb65",
                                                "text": "A system of communication called semaphore uses flags or flashing lights to send messages over distances. [...] Code flags are less common today but are sometimes used by ships that have lost radio contact."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b619d854-56da-45ab-881e-6c20dd3441c1",
                                                "sense_id": "d58b7504-1253-3337-851b-5427ed53bb65",
                                                "text": "As always in Lisbon, my heart throbbed semaphores to call Tónio."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e49bd9a7-9c3c-49bb-be06-040e9af1d6b9",
                                                "sense_id": "d58b7504-1253-3337-851b-5427ed53bb65",
                                                "text": "Consider the wagging tail, the most basic semaphore in dog/human communication."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b53967ad-cc68-46d2-b156-0786cecebd5b",
                                                "sense_id": "d58b7504-1253-3337-851b-5427ed53bb65",
                                                "text": "Semaphore—a system of communicating over long distances by holding the arms or two flags in certain positions—is not a very efficient mode of communication for us. But for the Panamanian golden frog, semaphore is just the ticket. These frogs live near waterfalls, where the constant din renders vocal communication useless. [...] When they want to get someone else's attention, they flash pale patches of skin on their limbs or the webs between their toes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "47c5f65a-380f-4630-93f4-d862f06c9368",
                                                "sense_id": "d58b7504-1253-3337-851b-5427ed53bb65",
                                                "text": "For a half-hour episode, \"The Long Shadow\" was unusually complex, a web spun out of deception and equivocation that untangles when [Ronald] Reagan, transmitting his customized semaphores of concern (ridged brow, pursed lips, pained eyes), divulges the truth: [...]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a69f8a75-feeb-35e7-b146-2e4efd031d10",
                                        "entry_id": "239c840a-01a9-31e4-8d93-f73af7f7e715",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A bit, token, fragment of code, or some other mechanism which is used to restrict access to a shared function or device to a single process at a time, or to synchronize and coordinate events in different processes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6e76246-496b-41ed-92a0-bddadc2ef80d",
                                                "sense_id": "a69f8a75-feeb-35e7-b146-2e4efd031d10",
                                                "text": "The thread increments the semaphore to prevent other threads from entering the critical section at the same time."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "340c2874-e9ca-41af-9d30-4786083ec612",
                                                "sense_id": "a69f8a75-feeb-35e7-b146-2e4efd031d10",
                                                "text": "Several synchronization techniques have been proposed and many of them have been adopted by parallel and distributed operating systems or parallel programming platforms. [...] Semaphores represent another synchronization technique that is mainly used by traditional stand-alone operating systems."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b84c05df-d46a-4a11-b1e5-30f983b0f86a",
                                                "sense_id": "a69f8a75-feeb-35e7-b146-2e4efd031d10",
                                                "text": "A semaphore makes sure that the different processes don't step on each other's toes when they access the shared memory segment. Before a process can use the segment, it needs to get control of the semaphore. When it's done with the segment, it releases the semaphore for another process to grab."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "10e823cd-3124-4b9d-a95a-9e4959b154ca",
                                                "sense_id": "a69f8a75-feeb-35e7-b146-2e4efd031d10",
                                                "text": "It is up to the programmer to ensure that if one thread updates multiple dependent memory locations (for example, writing a string, or updating a table) that another thread might read, some protection is put in place to ensure that the two threads don't update and read at the same time. [...] Several techniques are used by programmers to prevent this, including locks, semaphores, and mutexes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "semaphore",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5c13f8dd-2ae6-3fb2-b13e-d58ffbadc52d",
                                        "entry_id": "c7cb7930-6cdf-3c4e-8d82-061016b39948",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To signal using, or as if using, a semaphore, with the implication that it is done nonverbally."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "ambitransitive",
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "04b68ea8-b6b8-46bf-854f-abf8e47b7aab",
                                                "sense_id": "5c13f8dd-2ae6-3fb2-b13e-d58ffbadc52d",
                                                "text": "The person intending to Semaphore will make the International Code Signal VOX (I am going to Semaphore to you), and set his Semaphore at the alphabetical sign [...] with the Indicator out, and wait until the person to whom the Semaphore signal is to be made hoists his answering pennant close up. [...] The British method of Semaphoring by flags held in the hand which is shown in plate VIII is exactly the same as the British Movable Semaphore system, which has just been explained, the positions of the apparatus which denote the letters, numbers, and special signs being, it will be seen, identical in each case, and the only difference being in the apparatus employed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5c7ab5ac-356a-421a-bf46-cbeaccf104c8",
                                                "sense_id": "5c13f8dd-2ae6-3fb2-b13e-d58ffbadc52d",
                                                "text": "These gunny-sack chaps are not animals or savages. Look, Henry! They are semaphoring! See that tree there, and that big one across the cañon. Watch the branches wave."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b40cf966-3f26-45bc-a5ef-22eb4a12926d",
                                                "sense_id": "5c13f8dd-2ae6-3fb2-b13e-d58ffbadc52d",
                                                "text": "Minutes later, unseen by the defenders, he semaphored back across the valley that he was going to make a fresh attempt."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ad550fc6-1b28-4cad-8259-bd8f5931dc52",
                                                "sense_id": "5c13f8dd-2ae6-3fb2-b13e-d58ffbadc52d",
                                                "text": "Near the concession stand on the east side of the park, she saw two familiar figures sitting on a bench in the shade of a large oak. Her father hailed her, wildly semaphoring with his hot dog."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a32ba53a-e155-46df-9cb0-4936c3c6fa00",
                                                "sense_id": "5c13f8dd-2ae6-3fb2-b13e-d58ffbadc52d",
                                                "text": "He can't hear what they're saying, but Jake is making angry movements with his hands and his taut posture semaphores, even to Daniel, his distinct displeasure."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e0143ba9-0ec7-4e04-8ca5-8d293975c529",
                                                "sense_id": "5c13f8dd-2ae6-3fb2-b13e-d58ffbadc52d",
                                                "text": "[Barack] Obama doesn't merely evince blackness; he uses his blackness to signal and court African Americans, semaphoring in a cultural dialect of our creation—crooning Al Green at the Apollo, name-checking Young Jeezy, regularly appearing on the cover of black magazines, weighing the merits of Jay-Z versus Kanye West, being photographed in the White House with a little black boy touching his hair."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4b06792a-390f-4cdc-859b-818d13829aab",
                        "source_entry_id": "f1f276a7-23db-3392-9c3b-86e1fc8196c1",
                        "target_lang_word": "Semaphor",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "92a783de-dccc-4946-889f-25345c2e94ec",
                        "source_entry_id": "f1f276a7-23db-3392-9c3b-86e1fc8196c1",
                        "target_lang_word": "opérateur",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "opérateur",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d6f0004f-d730-3835-97af-19dc33029b85",
                                        "entry_id": "dae1160d-8d3c-3ba0-8988-d36494c4baa9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Celui qui fait des opérations de chirurgie."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ffbbab31-5159-4683-9300-0387b0511341",
                                                "sense_id": "d6f0004f-d730-3835-97af-19dc33029b85",
                                                "text": "Mongicourt, dogmatique.– Une opération n’est jamais inutile. (Remettant l’étui dans sa poche.) Elle peut ne pas profiter à l’opéré… (Tirant une boîte d’allumettes de son gousset) elle profite toujours à l’opérateur.\nPetypon.– Tu es cynique !\nMongicourt, avec une moue d’indifférence professionnelle, tout en frottant son allumette.– Je suis chirurgien."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "63401733-18f1-4d8d-b389-0d9933d4eaf7",
                                                "sense_id": "d6f0004f-d730-3835-97af-19dc33029b85",
                                                "text": "Tel quel, il était un aigle à côté du prétentieux et roucoulant Pozzi dont l'ignorance en tout est fabuleuse, ou même de Doyen, opérateur génial, médiocre clinicien et qui s'imagine de temps en temps avoir découvert le remède de tous les maux."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a62bf0c3-05eb-4400-bdee-7cd5e5bff4de",
                                                "sense_id": "d6f0004f-d730-3835-97af-19dc33029b85",
                                                "text": "Mais cette Novelle marque une régression dans la voie de la répression de l’eunuchat. Estimant l'ancienne législation trop draconienne, Léon VI abolissait la peine du talion contre les opérateurs et adoucissait les autres pénalités."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0d2371ca-ba0e-3242-9c08-0c74021a867a",
                                        "entry_id": "dae1160d-8d3c-3ba0-8988-d36494c4baa9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ouvrier sur machine ; celui qui se livre à certaines manipulations pour faire fonctionner un appareil."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8d7f6595-527c-47da-8e1b-b052dfdd4d27",
                                                "sense_id": "0d2371ca-ba0e-3242-9c08-0c74021a867a",
                                                "text": "La principale difficulté demeure cependant la nettoyabilité. En effet, le lavage d'un box-dryer est une opération longue et difficile, réalisée manuellement par un opérateur qui doit entrer dans la chambre de séchage."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "75094e97-98b3-49b6-ac3d-51675a569c90",
                                                "sense_id": "0d2371ca-ba0e-3242-9c08-0c74021a867a",
                                                "text": "Le pot d’échappement a été supprimé sur le tracteur électrique, ce qui offre plus de visibilité à l’opérateur."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6352a337-ee0a-3a97-8f67-037c3c24d024",
                                        "entry_id": "dae1160d-8d3c-3ba0-8988-d36494c4baa9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Cadreur."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "383a00ad-fbaf-36d8-aa98-402e9ec877ae",
                                        "entry_id": "dae1160d-8d3c-3ba0-8988-d36494c4baa9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Charlatan, vendeur de médications sans effet, bonimenteur."
                                        ],
